,"winningTimeRank":15,"winningTimeRankDir":5,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["up"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:30:12","holder":"Bruce FORDYCE","year":1983,"type":"up"},"womenRecords":["overall"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"06:44:35","holder":"Isavel ROCHE-KELLY","year":1981,"type":"overall"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1956,"mensWinner":"Gerald WALSH","mensTime":"06:33:35"}},"narrative":"The 1988 Comrades Marathon was the 63rd running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 87.500 km. The race was held on Tuesday, 31 May. Conditions: Cool morning warming to hot cloudless day. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:27:42, ahead of Mark PAGE (05:38:28) and Nick BESTER (05:39:00). Frith VAN DER MERWE won the women's race in 06:32:56, followed by Lettie GREEFF (07:04:00).\n\nBruce FORDYCE's 05:27:42 broke FORDYCE's own up record of 05:30:12 set in 1983. Frith VAN DER MERWE set a new women's course record of 06:32:56, surpassing Isavel ROCHE-KELLY's 06:44:35 from 1981. Frith VAN DER MERWE's 06:32:56 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1956 (Gerald WALSH, 06:33:35).\n\nFrom a field of 12,292 entries, 10,357 runners crossed the finish line (84.3% completion rate), with athletes representing over 18 countries. The field comprised 9,813 men and 544 women (5.3% female). The average finish time was 09:25:04.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 967 Silver, 9,377 Bronze. 3,228 runners (31.2%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Nico DE BEER in 10:59:58.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1987, the field was 13.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 22% of the finishers, with 8,076 seniors (avg 09:23:22) and 2,279 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}